WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.020
Two identical triangles fit together to make a

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.440
parallelogram, and a parallelogram has the same area as

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.590
a rectangle with the same base and height.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.470
So a triangle's area is half its base times its height.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.160
The height must be measured straight up from the base,

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.630
at a right angle.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.380
The most common error is using a slanted side

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.130
as the height.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.380
The second most common is trying to measure an awkward

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.560
shape directly, when it would be far easier to subtract

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.330
simple shapes from a rectangle.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.070
Three triangles share a base of eight centimetres.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.640
Their top corners lie at different places along a line

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.810
parallel to the base, five centimetres above it.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.150
Which triangle has the largest area?

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.410
Pause and think about the height of each.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.950
Every one of them has height five, because the top

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.660
corners are all five centimetres above the base.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.060
Half of eight times five is twenty.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.860
All three have the same area: twenty square centimetres.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.770
Sliding the top corner along a parallel line changes the

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.640
shape, but not the area.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.820
Now an awkward triangle inside a six by four rectangle.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.760
Its sides are all slanted.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.360
Do not attack it directly.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.820
The rectangle has area twenty-four.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.180
Around the triangle are three right-angled triangles,

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.720
with areas nine, four and two.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.340
Those three take up fifteen.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.540
Twenty-four minus fifteen leaves nine.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:31.460
The awkward triangle has area nine square centimetres.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.570
Subtracting the surroundings is called

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.560
using the complement.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.990
One more useful fact.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.740
Join any point on the top edge of a rectangle to

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.710
both bottom corners.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.780
The triangle has the rectangle's base and the

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.860
rectangle's height, so it is always exactly half the

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.830
rectangle, wherever the point is.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.250
Half base times perpendicular height.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.900
Triangles with the same base and height have

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.770
the same area.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.490
For awkward shapes, subtract from a rectangle.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.660
Notebook challenge: a triangle has base ten centimetres

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.310
and area thirty-five square centimetres.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:06.870
What is its height?
